        "original_id": "93e04e9c-af12-5cef-939f-cefc14cd86c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mel Brooks, Charles Durning, Alan Johnson, Carol Kane, Fred Walton\n- Films: To Be or Not to Be, When a Stranger Calls Back, When a Stranger Calls, The Sting, Dog Day Afternoon, The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas, Tootsie\n- Topics: film roles, film production, sequels\n\nFacts:\n- Mel Brooks was born as Melvin Kaminsky on June 28, 1926, and he is an American actor, writer, producer, director, comedian, and composer.\n- Charles Durning's best-known film roles included The Sting in 1973 and Dog Day Afternoon in 1975.\n- Charles Durning's best-known comedy roles included The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas in 1982, Tootsie in 1982, and To Be or Not to Be in 1983.\n- To Be or Not to Be is a 1983 American war comedy film directed by Alan Johnson and produced by Mel Brooks.\n- When a Stranger Calls Back is a 1993 American made-for-television psychological horror film and a sequel to the 1979 film When a Stranger Calls.\n- When a Stranger Calls Back reunited Carol Kane and Charles Durning, reprising Jill Johnson and John Clifford, with director Fred Walton from the original film.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
